※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4920 LANG_ENTRY_TAKES_A_PARAMETER

※ One name and nothing else.  An expression would have to be worked out at
※ entry and its answer carried through the body, which is the cost an `old` has
※ and this does not -- so what may be written is the thing that is already
※ there.

fn step(a: u8) → u8 post(⎕entry(a ⊞ a) > 0u8):
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(step(1u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
